      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-01T07:52:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be good to document the order (root to leaf or v.v.?)\n\nAlso, does this just have multiple certificates concatenated?  Would it be easier for consumers to have the distinct certs separate?",
      "revId": "7fe2d43b5f14b2526187915d4dd6940c430eec39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d5f27fea_d014fa8e",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/aidl/android/system/virtualization/payload/IVmPayloadService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T13:09:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is more than just a concatenation of certificates; it is intended to be a certificate chain. In this chain, each certificate\u0027s private key signs the next certificate. The root certificate is trusted by Google, and the leaf certificate includes the public key that corresponds to the private key, as outlined in the DD [1].\n\nI added this to the doc.\n\n[1] http://doc/1SetVcA-i6MyyWpgXc1fULkklDAUsOQBVYpYJfspfsF8#heading\u003dh.6yrugcqgy0gn \u003e Diagram: Extending the Google-backed certificate chain with a new certificate after client VM attestation",
      "parentUuid": "11b20340_162e3ab8",
      "revId": "7fe2d43b5f14b2526187915d4dd6940c430eec39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d8534e6_0b6e3ab6",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/aidl/android/system/virtualization/payload/IVmPayloadService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T17:06:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nonetheless, would it be easier for client id we represent this as a byte[][], so each cert is separate?\n\n(We will also need to define the cert extension in the final cert that describes the payload, but that is for the future.)",
      "parentUuid": "d5f27fea_d014fa8e",
      "revId": "7fe2d43b5f14b2526187915d4dd6940c430eec39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a693b52_ffe40b94",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/aidl/android/system/virtualization/payload/IVmPayloadService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T11:42:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Done.\n\n`byte[][]` doesn\u0027t compile with error:\n```\nERROR: packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid_manager/aidl/android/system/virtualization/payload/IVmPayloadService.aidl:54.27-63.15: Multi-dimensional arrays must be fixed size.\n```\nI added a `Certificate` wrapping the `byte[]`. think it\u0027s more clear.\n\nBut I\u0027m not sure how we should return a nested vector to client in the NDK API?",
      "parentUuid": "8d8534e6_0b6e3ab6",
      "revId": "7fe2d43b5f14b2526187915d4dd6940c430eec39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3f24672_cc92a418",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/aidl/android/system/virtualization/payload/IVmPayloadService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T11:56:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. Well, the question was, what is easier for clients?\nAt one level separating out the certs seems helpful.\nOTOH I suspect most clients will just send the cert somewhere - e.g. to the app and thence to some server - where the actual parsing and verification will have to happen. So perhaps just a flat array of bytes is easier. It is certainly easier to expose as a C API.\n\n@drysdale@google.com might have an opinion.",
      "parentUuid": "1a693b52_ffe40b94",
      "revId": "7fe2d43b5f14b2526187915d4dd6940c430eec39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4a280d43_105716a0",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/aidl/android/system/virtualization/payload/IVmPayloadService.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 25
      },
      "lineNbr": 57,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-06T08:05:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d lean towards separating the certs, because not all X.509 libraries have a convenient entrypoint for dealing with concatenated DER certs (e.g. [Go does](https://pkg.go.dev/crypto/x509#ParseCertificates) but the Rust `x509-cert` crate only copes with [concatenated PEM format](https://docs.rs/x509-cert/latest/x509_cert/certificate/struct.CertificateInner.html#method.load_pem_chain), and I\u0027m not sure about [BoringSSL](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/boringssl/src/crypto/x509/x_x509.c?q\u003d%22d2i_X509%28%22)).\n\nIt\u0027s much easier to concatenate DER data than it is to separate it...",
      "parentUuid": "e3f24672_cc92a418",
      "revId": "7fe2d43b5f14b2526187915d4dd6940c430eec39",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
